bishop on c8 toward White’s king after c3 is attacked. It also restricts White’s minor pieces. Given Black’s development lead (knights out vs White’s knights on b1/g1 still at home), opening the center favors the better-developed side. This move also prevents White from comfortably playing e4 later.\n\n**Answer:** P: d5-d4"}
