he white king has only limited escape squares (e2, f3, f4, d2), we could gain time to push pawns or coordinate knight/king. White cannot capture the rook (no piece can). This move also possibly leads to skewer or discovered checks if the king moves and we reposition the rook. Given material, forcing the white king to retreat allows us to advance the c-pawn or activate the knight more effectively.  \n\n**Answer:** R: d4-d3"}
