est win is to queen a pawn. Pushing a5-a4 immediately gets the pawn closer to promotion, and with the knight and king able to come support, White’s king cannot catch it in time. After a5-a4, White’s only move is king moves, then Black can play a4-a3, then a3-a2, etc. The knight can also deliver checks to distract White’s king. The knight move N: c2-e3 is tempting for activity, but promoting a pawn is simpler and decisive. Given the huge material advantage, converting a pawn is the most straightforward path to checkmate.\n\nAnswer: P: a5-a4"}
