 the most forcing is **N: e1-c2**, because it immediately attacks White king and gains tempo.  \n\nReason for final choice: In endgame up material, activate pieces and force opponent’s king into bad position. Nc2 attacks White king, forcing it to move (likely to a1, cornering it), then Black can bring king to b3 or c3 to support pawn advance and create mating threats with knight and king. This is more active than pawn moves which might allow White king to get active.  \n\nAnswer: N: e1-c2'}
