ite king can capture (Kb1xa2) unless we protect it. Moving knight to a1 gives check, forcing white king to c1, after which we can bring our king closer to support pawn promotion. Alternatively, we could move king first to support the pawn (Kd4-c3), then push pawn to a2 with protection. However, Nc2-a1 is more forcing and creates immediate pressure; after Kb1-c1, we can play Kd4-c3, then push a3-a2 with king protection, and white king is confined to the corner. This sequence seems efficient.\n\nTherefore, I choose **N: c2-a1**.\n\nAnswer: N: c2-a1"}
