3 pawn can move later. King can follow to support. It’s better than moving a3 first because then a5 stays blocked. **K: b3-a4** also good, but moving pawn first gains tempo and fixes pawn structure. After a5-a4, black can play Kb3-a4 next turn, protecting a4 pawn while white king is stuck dealing with promotion threat. So a5-a4 is the most forcing and progressive move.\n\nAnswer: P: a5-a4'}
